# How to cite Vote Lab (PLAN_BEYOND_CI W2.5). The Polity run archive gets its own DOI when it is
# uploaded to Zenodo; add it here as an `identifiers` entry then.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its simulation data, please cite it as below."
title: "Vote Lab: a voting-theory sandbox and Polity, an LLM-agent democracy simulator"
type: software
authors:
  - alias: Burbanit0
repository-code: "https://github.com/Burbanit0/Vote-App"
license: MIT
version: 0.2.0
date-released: "2026-09-27"
keywords:
  - social choice
  - voting methods
  - electoral systems
  - agent-based simulation
  - large language models
abstract: >-
  Vote Lab shows that the choice of voting method changes the winner: 29 methods in a
  browser playground and a FastAPI engine, 28 of them locked together across the two
  implementations by a parity test. Polity simulates a democracy whose citizens, party
  leaders and presidents can be played by a language model; in those runs every model call
  is logged, and the run can be replayed from the log.
